    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47f68f6f_fde8b402",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawWriter.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-31T20:41:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I haven\u0027t completely isolated what is going on, but I think without modifying setTemplate, we end up in a situation where we thrash between static vertex buffers and dynamic vertex buffers as pipelines switch. \n\nOne thought that is immediately applicable that might simplify some of this tracking is instead of having: fVertices, fInstances, fPendingBufferBinds, and fPendingBaseInstance|Vertex, we switch to tracking: fBoundVertices, fBoundInstances, fPendingVertices, fPendingInstances.\n\nThen in flush, we can look at the byte offset of the pending vertex and instance buffers (and also index buffer offset), and try and shift them into one the draw call parameters to get to a canonical binding BindBufferInfo (ideally with offset \u003d 0).  Then if those are different from the `fBoundFoo`s, we record the binding command before the draw command.\n\nI think that simplifies what needs to happen in setTemplate (just flushes on change to pending BBIs) and newPipelineState (reset pending BBIs) because of the built-in stride alignments that the BoundsManager is doing. Inside flush() we\u0027ll typically being seeing everything at the alignment that the pipeline wants.\n\n\nThe other issue that just realized could be happening is when the pipelines are switching between vertex-appended data and instance-appended data.  Instead of being able to bind both kinds of appendable data to one slot, and separately keep the static data bound to another slot, we are thrashing the vertex binding between the static VBO and the dynamic VBO.  I think we can chat tomorrow about what this might look like, and outline a plan to make the different parts of this growing change landable and reviewable in isolation.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "2ae2f31a81736b63f72824162e6a096381b4ad92",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    }
